{"sha":"a42ac8daf4b86e8d41ed01518bf6b3e1a35b5071","node_id":"C_kwDODI9FZdoAKGE0MmFjOGRhZjRiODZlOGQ0MWVkMDE1MThiZjZiM2UxYTM1YjUwNzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Kevin Jones","email":"kevin@vcsjones.com","date":"2026-11-21T02:28:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-11-21T02:28:40Z"},"message":"Prioritize loading OpenSSL 4.x\n\n1. OpenSSL 3.x was preferentially loaded before 4.x because at the time\n4.x was not stable. That is no longer true, so lets' probe for OpenSSL\n4.x first, and prefer it if both are present.\n2. The OpenBSD and FreeBSD SO names were not present for OpenSSL 4.1\nfrom Ports, so let's catch them up.\n* FreeBSD 4.0\nhttps://cgit.freebsd.org/ports/plain/security/openssl40/version.mk\n* FreeBSD 4.1\nhttps://cgit.freebsd.org/ports/plain/security/openssl41/version.mk\n* OpenBSD 4.0\nhttps://cvsweb.openbsd.org/checkout/ports/security/openssl/4.0/Makefile?rev=HEAD&content-type=text/plain\n* OpenBSD 4.1\nhttps://cvsweb.openbsd.org/checkout/ports/security/openssl/4.1/Makefile?rev=HEAD&content-type=text/plain\n    \nRecall that OpenBSD loads by directory name, not by an SONAME suffix,\nthen by highest SHLIBVER in the directory.\n3. OpenSSL from 3.6 via Ports was also missing, so let's add it. It's no\nlonger supported, but FreeBSD still has it with an SONAME suffix of 18.\nhttps://cgit.freebsd.org/ports/plain/security/openssl36/version.mk","tree":{"sha":"356b4f4d351b489f2bf4309b900911f915037273","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/runtime/git/trees/356b4f4d351b489f2bf4309b900911f915037273"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/runtime/git/commits/a42ac8daf4b86e8d41ed01518bf6b3e1a35b5071","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJrAQHYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsSYQAGvgP2TOktzofQGHbUD5hdgV\n3cY9UCcdqYx8hoMUukQQvd7KJWAw6ivtVBD0Qx0j22KQv0vsnzIJgMfiNA0JdiX9\nURe4CQw17Kjc40g/FAWKY6Wo5NmmWn69foAfU0uykTXzGdCxBBwhdSwt49Z7Wud8\nUTbZVXUSENBYa3h0Es4p68A/56SUjE5NWeUdyFxS8eD+fTvgzGVnD87mDeQKy43F\nnpeBhWi75oZMBwhOhsSfC3vOOJKDf4PZEqGLHQtVGR+F+u/5y3X3dyMFLtqNymuD\nig62MGKD4S/wx+CD/GbebVdiKX5wWlpghUmKyz2dQ6T9N+4sowtNls1RCKEw4E56\nLqA0MHNiZ8ciE+0zoKi/AXpjpbcY2kgzn0XyK+VXwPw2FLjwISmDH708hTsH54aF\npu6I/UHYWddoZTEA79214Y/2YOICyth9qFrct+GR7z/UkxGHycybc3k1u5QoADhd\nj7yF3nxb+mrRJXzPGiCk8r7jTAjh9HG+hf2UPs0qfXpLO1mi5vvkmyi5pyAlY5tm\nPYkBYZUtQ8snpDZ0/4Mx1NU1HTpRjqFK5nf5CXJUeScVpN9CpyWMZSL7iGifkj9y\nph80+gk4DfV+kBxpFRsMMmIidoFM0lgAS8pC5996/yhQtFgHGoVtNt4SrNRZLNur\n9OEbUVSJUTfYte6fkr/g\n=dBSf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 356b4f4d351b489f2bf4309b900911f915037273\nparent e8e8e319862f41b5c7d92f23096a3df872701ede\nauthor Kevin Jones <kevin@vcsjones.com> 1795228120 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1795228120 -0500\n\nPrioritize loading OpenSSL 4.x\n\n1. OpenSSL 3.x was preferentially loaded before 4.x because at the time\n4.x was not stable. That is no longer true, so lets' probe for OpenSSL\n4.x first, and prefer it if both are present.\n2. The OpenBSD and FreeBSD SO names were not present for OpenSSL 4.1\nfrom Ports, so let's catch them up.\n* FreeBSD 4.0\nhttps://cgit.freebsd.org/ports/plain/security/openssl40/version.mk\n* FreeBSD 4.1\nhttps://cgit.freebsd.org/ports/plain/security/openssl41/version.mk\n* OpenBSD 4.0\nhttps://cvsweb.openbsd.org/checkout/ports/security/openssl/4.0/Makefile?rev=HEAD&content-type=text/plain\n* OpenBSD 4.1\nhttps://cvsweb.openbsd.org/checkout/ports/security/openssl/4.1/Makefile?rev=HEAD&content-type=text/plain\n    \nRecall that OpenBSD loads by directory name, not by an SONAME suffix,\nthen by highest SHLIBVER in the directory.\n3. OpenSSL from 3.6 via Ports was also missing, so let's add it. It's no\nlonger supported, but FreeBSD still has it with an SONAME suffix of 18.\nhttps://cgit.freebsd.org/ports/plain/security/openssl36/version.mk","verified_at":"2026-11-21T02:28:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/runtime/commits/a42ac8daf4b86e8d41ed01518bf6b3e1a35b5071","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/commit/a42ac8daf4b86e8d41ed01518bf6b3e1a35b5071","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/runtime/commits/a42ac8daf4b86e8d41ed01518bf6b3e1a35b5071/comments","author":{"login":"vcsjones","id":361677,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MTY3Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/361677?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcsjones","html_url":"https://github.com/vcsjones","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcsjones/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcsjones/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcsjones/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcsjones/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcsjones/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcsjones/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcsjones/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcsjones/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vcsjones/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e8e8e319862f41b5c7d92f23096a3df872701ede","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/runtime/commits/e8e8e319862f41b5c7d92f23096a3df872701ede","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/commit/e8e8e319862f41b5c7d92f23096a3df872701ede"}],"stats":{"total":46,"additions":31,"deletions":15},"files":[{"sha":"52950fc78ec76b51537cf7c8d327818626bd9537","filename":"src/native/libs/System.Security.Cryptography.Native/opensslshim.c","status":"modified","additions":31,"deletions":15,"changes":46,"blob_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/a42ac8daf4b86e8d41ed01518bf6b3e1a35b5071/src%2Fnative%2Flibs%2FSystem.Security.Cryptography.Native%2Fopensslshim.c","raw_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/raw/a42ac8daf4b86e8d41ed01518bf6b3e1a35b5071/src%2Fnative%2Flibs%2FSystem.Security.Cryptography.Native%2Fopensslshim.c","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/runtime/contents/src%2Fnative%2Flibs%2FSystem.Security.Cryptography.Native%2Fopensslshim.c?ref=a42ac8daf4b86e8d41ed01518bf6b3e1a35b5071","patch":"@@ -169,6 +169,24 @@ static void OpenLibraryOnce(void)\n     }\n #elif defined(__FreeBSD__)\n     // The ports version of OpenSSL is used over base where possible\n+    if (libssl == NULL)\n+    {\n+        // OpenSSL 4.1 from ports\n+        DlOpen(MAKELIB(\"20\"));\n+    }\n+\n+    if (libssl == NULL)\n+    {\n+        // OpenSSL 4.0 from ports\n+        DlOpen(MAKELIB(\"19\"));\n+    }\n+\n+    if (libssl == NULL)\n+    {\n+        // OpenSSL 3.6 from ports\n+        DlOpen(MAKELIB(\"18\"));\n+    }\n+\n     if (libssl == NULL)\n     {\n         // OpenSSL 3.5 from ports\n@@ -203,15 +221,21 @@ static void OpenLibraryOnce(void)\n     {\n         DlOpen(MAKELIB(\"111\"));\n     }\n+#elif defined(__OpenBSD__)\n+    // OpenBSD base is LibreSSL; load the OpenSSL ports build from /usr/local/lib/eopenssl<NN>.\n+    // Probe the known package directories explicitly, newest versions first.\n+    if (libssl == NULL)\n+    {\n+        // OpenSSL 4.1 from ports\n+        DlOpenEOpenSsl(\"41\");\n+    }\n \n-    // OpenSSL 4 from ports is probed last, but not preferred.\n     if (libssl == NULL)\n     {\n-        DlOpen(MAKELIB(\"19\"));\n+        // OpenSSL 4.0 from ports\n+        DlOpenEOpenSsl(\"40\");\n     }\n-#elif defined(__OpenBSD__)\n-    // OpenBSD base is LibreSSL; load the OpenSSL ports build from /usr/local/lib/eopenssl<NN>.\n-    // Probe the known package directories explicitly, preferring 3.x and trying 4.0 last.\n+\n     if (libssl == NULL)\n     {\n         // OpenSSL 3.6 from ports\n@@ -223,30 +247,22 @@ static void OpenLibraryOnce(void)\n         // OpenSSL 3.5 from ports\n         DlOpenEOpenSsl(\"35\");\n     }\n+#endif\n \n     if (libssl == NULL)\n     {\n-        // OpenSSL 4.0 from ports (probed but not preferred)\n-        DlOpenEOpenSsl(\"40\");\n+        DlOpen(MAKELIB(\"4\"));\n     }\n-#endif\n \n     if (libssl == NULL)\n     {\n-        // Prefer OpenSSL 3.x\n         DlOpen(MAKELIB(\"3\"));\n     }\n \n     if (libssl == NULL)\n     {\n         DlOpen(MAKELIB(\"1.1\"));\n     }\n-\n-    // While it's still in alpha, OpenSSL 4 is probed, but not preferred.\n-    if (libssl == NULL)\n-    {\n-        DlOpen(MAKELIB(\"4\"));\n-    }\n }\n \n static pthread_once_t g_openLibrary = PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT;"}]}